# What is stored is the project's business. What is checked out is the
# contributor's, and this file deliberately leaves it alone except in one place.
#
# The reason is that this project's fixtures are bytes that have to be exact. A
# filter that rewrites a line ending on the way into git destroys the thing a
# fixture exists to prove, and it says nothing while doing it. So every type the
# tree carries is declared here rather than left to a heuristic that guesses
# right until the day it does not.
#
# There is no `eol=` on the text lines below, apart from the shell scripts. A
# working tree with carriage returns is not the fault this guards against, and
# forcing every checkout to LF would hide the fault instead of refusing it: the
# check in .github/workflows/line-endings.yml reads what is stored, so a
# contributor whose platform checks out CRLF gets a green run on an unmodified
# tree. CONTRIBUTING.md carries the command that shows it.

# The default. Git decides text from content and normalises what it decides is
# text, so anything not named below still lands with LF stored.
* text=auto

# Text, by type. `diff=` picks the hunk-header driver where git ships one, so a
# diff says which function or which section it landed in.
*.py            text diff=python
*.md            text diff=markdown
*.toml          text
*.yml           text
*.yaml          text
*.json          text
*.cfg           text
*.ini           text
*.txt           text
*.lock          text
.gitattributes  text
.gitignore      text
.editorconfig   text
DCO             text
LICENSE         text

# The one working-tree declaration. A carriage return in a shell script is not
# untidiness: it lands inside the shebang line and the interpreter is not found,
# with an error naming a file that plainly exists.
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Binary, by type. No line-ending filter, no textual diff, no merge attempt. The
# image types are what an editing pipeline is tested against; the model artefact
# types are what a registry entry will point at.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.bmp           binary
*.tif           binary
*.tiff          binary
*.webp          binary
*.avif          binary
*.heic          binary
*.heif          binary
*.ico           binary
*.safetensors   binary
*.onnx          binary
*.ckpt          binary
*.pt            binary
*.pth           binary
*.npy           binary
*.npz           binary
*.bin           binary
*.gguf          binary

# Fixture for the near-miss proof, removed in the commit after it.
fixture-crlf.txt -text
